{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1549799-mage-the-ascension-campaign-ideas","id":1549799,"title":"Mage the Ascension - Campaign Ideas","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2025-04-03T19:08:05-07:00","id":1549799,"title":"<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/icons/icon5.png\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" alt=\"\" /> Mage the Ascension - Campaign Ideas","content":"I'm getting back into running MtAw after a long hiatus, and I was really curious to hear what people thought might be some good ideas for overall campaign stories. <br /> <br /> As a matter of preference, I far prefer to run games in which the individual character back stories are the driving force for the game. In this case, I'm looking to come up with an idea for a campaign and then help the players tailor their characters to it (with the potential for substantial side stories as well. One of my absolute most hated GM sins is when they neither know nor care about the PCs and try to ramrod them through their plot.)<br /> <br /> Some things I'd like to avoid:<ol class=\"decimal\"><li>Campaign ideas that start off with the players captured or otherwise forced into something against their will. Most people acknowledge this as the worst opening move in a majority of cases.</li> <li>Ideas which involve the God-Machine. I'm not a fan, personally.</li> </ol><br /> Really interested to hear what thoughts people have. Heck, if you just want to gush about your campaign (even if you or the GM used the things I'd like to avoid) I'd love to hear it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>We don't allow mages to cast spells, since this is the most unbalancing rule of all.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5226-jachra","name":"Jachra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5226_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-04-03T22:13:32-07:00","id":1549804,"title":"","content":"Thing To Avoid #1 is, of course, giving me the idea of a Mystery wherein one or more of the PCs somehow have memories of the Captivity undergone by the proto-Tremere, or possibly the Invoked Veil cabal that stood watch over the fortress of Chur where the Tremere freed the Seventh Dragon. (The Tremere, of course, would have an interest in this for multiple obvious reasons.)<br /> <br /> For a less invasive mechanism than putting potential past-life memories in the PCs' heads, one could take everybody's favorite sideways juke from the Standard Model and have these memories instead be contained in what changelings would recognize as Icons (stabilized through pledgecraft to exist outside the Hedge).<br /> <br /> To split the difference via Geist, perhaps they're capital-M Memories retained by a ghost using the mechanics provided for the Absent, or identifiers retrieved from the Ocean of Fragments at the bottom of the Underworld rendered into Mementos via a long trip up to a River City market and somehow winding up in an occultist's collection for whatever minor supernatural power they have as a peripheral effect.<br /> <br /> Thing To Avoid #2, of course, can also combine with this concept by virtue of the fact that messing with memories by concrete means is a thing the Unchained can do through memory pacts (described in Dark Eras 2's Empire of Gold and Dust chapter) and more conventional Cover patchwork, either of which necessarily creates and is sustained by readable documentation (barring the use of the methods for Pacts in a Pre-Literate World in Dark Eras 1's Beneath the Skin chapter) that is supernaturally more durable than the material would normally be.<br /> <br /> tl;dr &quot;A couple thousand years ago the mages who would become the Tremere were in a nightmarish situationship with assorted gods and monsters in the pursuit of arcane power and knowledge of the soul. The PCs find themselves in literal or figurative possession of the memories of one or more parties to That Time Power-Hungry Wizards Bound And Were Bound By Supernatural Beings And Broke Their Souls, and even if that doesn't pique their curiosity and/or fear, someone or something is after them because of that association.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-04-05T15:45:28-07:00","id":1549851,"title":"","content":"The cabal starts getting messages from their loved ones. On the TV when it has a sudden burst of static, on the radio, on their phones or PCs. They swear they never called them, and magic reveals this is true. Each message leads them to an impending danger, an important event. Even loved ones long lost may call.<br /> <br /> Sometimes its the voice of an old man, reading coordinates slowly, deliberately. They always correspond to real world places, always leading to a cold case, even supernatural ones. Sometimes they are decades or centuries apart, other times they are from those that happened that very week.<br /> <br /> Something hurt the timeline, and its up to them to decipher what caused these scars of time.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-04-06T13:35:00-07:00","id":1549882,"title":"","content":"Do you need one backstory to unite them all, or just some way to unite few backstories? Or do you need backstory which will push the campaign?<br /> Anyway, here are few sketches.<br /> <br /> <b>Acanthus:</b><ul><li>For a months you see omens of events too distant and derived from your everyday life. Yet, last week you felt deja vu - something at the periphery, an old couple; you heard their quarrel, but not only when you went near them - you knew that quarrel year before, reasons for it, result, words... you forgot it as a dream, again. Yet, you frequently noticed them, at some point your memories started failing you - your routine looks the same way, people speak the same or similar things. Did they speak it before or are you just tired? For all you know - days are moving. Was this a memory erased and returned? A warning? Or have you lived this all before? Will it lead you to anything?<ul><li>Is mage trapped in endless routine? Or does fate send us a messages? Or maybe we are in timeloop, we just don't realize it yet.</li> </ul></li> </ul><ul><li>Witch: You had someone. You played with your powers to uncover mystery, and you succeeded, saved people, make them better. But in the end, you was forced to make a simple choice between many and one. You magic warped everything once more, these time erasing previous chain of causality and events, your actions. You try to not remember those who you left, who are no longer connected to you, someone from who you strip whole future. Closest did suffer, and yet no one will appreciate sacrifice. You still can't understand why or how those events were connected; why only such sacrifice will work? how did it start? You tried to cheat a fate - it never worked even when nothing should ever intervene, you were there many times with the same choice; there are no one to ask. And yet, months after you`re tormented by haunting visions of reality where you succeeded, wasn't forced to sacrifice anyone. It is a happy place, your dream which are no longer real. Is it a destiny or madness?<ul><li>Classic Time/Fate moment - anomaly which somehow overcome your plan and powers and forces you to make a sacrifice. And like salt on your wounds, you see what you could have if only you found a way to overcome that mystery.</li> </ul></li> </ul><br /> <br /> <b>Mastigos:</b><br /> <b>Everyday Samaritan</b> ~ You are a warlock, world knew many like you - <u>manipulative bastards</u>; But wait, of course, <u><b>you</b></u> are different, you would never go into someone`s mind to secretly dig secrets, or endlessly survey their life. Sometimes you just check them, just to be sure that nothing is wrong. You are their best friend, you tries to use your gift as a tool to make their life better, fix their problems. You are always here for them, always there when they have a problems, always right there to suggest solution, always have something capable to fix their problem... you almost never asked a thanks or anything, and your kind soul help them in almost any time (when they come to you directly).<br /> Do you like their frustrated faces? Do you really thought that no one will notice how fast you moved from one side of the town to another? How conveniently fast you gathered exactly those documents, how fast you convinced another people, or how you suggested only working with a few people will be a right choice which will not lead to problems - how far is that from a threat? You helped many to fix their problems, but what if you are the source of their misery?<ul><li>Its art of miscommunication ~ just keep record of all players actions. Then drop in some time-table, and look at it from the perspective of others. Bonus point if player/pc has low social stats. Now time to blame.</li> <li>Its not like a typical campaign, but you can use it as additional element in story or between important parts of your main story.</li> <li>Originally it was a situation of mastigos with high Space / low Mind - they knew too many things which were hidden. Plus, if no one remember magic, but they knew you fixed their hard problem - they start asking a questions.</li> </ul><b>The Hole in Your Reflection</b> ~ Every mirror lies. You\u2019ve known that since your Awakening. But now, the reflections are different - they hesitate when you move, blink when your eyes remain still, smile when you don\u2019t. Something inside the glass is watching, waiting, growing closer. It knows your secrets. Worse, it knows what you could become, the versions of you that <u><b>should </b></u>have existed. And it wants to trade places.<ul><li>Mekhet vibe. | It could be anything, your demon, alter-you, agent of the Exarchs, or insanity.</li> </ul><br /> <br /> <b>Universal (for most gamelines):</b><br /> <b>Heritage</b>: You had large family, with curious traditions; One by one they left you, until there were only a few, and even they met strange untimely end. One night you received a small package - inside, there were letter to you parents, small box full of unknown coins (maybe, one of your relative was a collector), old keys and documents, an old diary full of names and instructions - it depicts things from someone's imagination. You do not believe in gods, curses or any forces (even if your family were convinced otherwise), yet you keep that feeling - need to move. No longer bound by anyone, you did what you can - keep low profile, be unnoticed. Something is following you and you know officials will not help you; whatever you have from your inheritance - it can't protect you forever. You're not sure what happened, but maybe you can get answers in the legacy of your family.<ul><li>These backstory can be used by anyone, because you try to investigate / avoid mystery for your own safety. Perfect for mortals with few supernatural merits - have no will or powers to fight, yet will resist as much as they can. Easy to modify for any gameline.</li> <li>You have a diary with a list of unknown creatures, names and something else. Let's imagine some ghostly figure, it brings you a messages or items and always asks some payment in rare artifacts (and have only few of them from your family' stash). You can avoid them, keep yourself near people, in public space - but ghost has a patience, he will wait until you are alone and no mundane lock will protect you. You have no connection or friend to help you there. You don't know who sends letters or why. And if life ever could be better, you are hunted by another creatures, for what you care - you just hide and run.</li> <li><i><b>Plus, ST is not forced to drop 10 uber-spirits every day/scene/turn.</b></i></li> </ul>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25408-alphari","name":"Alphari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25408_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"153"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}